# Databench settings. Copy this file to `.env` and set one key below.
#
# `docker compose up` needs nothing else. Every other line is optional, with
# its default shown, and is described where it is declared, in
# packages/api-core/alkera_core/config.py. One KEY=value per line, and never a
# comment on the same line as a value. Never commit a real value.

# --- Required ---
# One model provider key. The gateway uses it for every organisation; an
# organisation admin can add their own keys later.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# --- Developing (`make dev-all`; the docker compose stack sets its own) ---
# `make bootstrap` copies this file to `.env`; `make` then writes this
# checkout's ports to .env.workspace, and .env.local holds your overrides.
# local runs with development secrets and no TLS. production refuses insecure
# settings at boot.
APP_ENV=local
API_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000
# FRONTEND_BASE_URL=http://localhost:5173
API_CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173
API_HOST=127.0.0.1
# The port `make dev-backend` serves the API on (read by the Makefile, not the app).
API_PORT=8000
# Email (invitations, password resets) needs an SMTP relay.
EMAIL_ENABLED=true
SMTP_HOST=localhost
SMTP_PORT=1025
SMTP_FROM=no-reply@localhost
# SMTP_USERNAME=
# SMTP_PASSWORD=
# A directory to generate and keep the server secrets in (see the README).
# GENERATED_SECRETS_DIR=

# --- Local development ---
# Values the local stack (`make infra-up`, `make dev-all`) runs with.
DATABASE_POOL_PRESSURE_LOG_INTERVAL_SECONDS=10
FILES_GC_ENABLED=false
FILES_STORE_PROVIDER=s3_compatible
FILES_STORE_BUCKET=alkera-files
FILES_STORE_ACCESS_KEY=alkera
FILES_STORE_SECRET_KEY=alkera-dev-secret

# --- Optional ---
# The defaults below are what an unset name means.

# App
# LOG_LEVEL=INFO
# METRICS_ENABLED=true
# METRICS_AUTH_TOKEN=
# LOG_SYSLOG_ENDPOINT=

# API
# FORWARDED_FOR_TRUSTED_HOPS=1
# GATE_INGEST_MAX_BODY_BYTES=34603008
# REQUEST_SCAN_MAX_BODY_BYTES=2097152
# GATE_MAX_ACTIVE_CI_TOKENS_PER_ORG=25

# DB
